  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable Energy Services for Education and Health in Afghanistan (SESEHA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Health facilities and services improved through reliable access to electricity. As per the SESEHA project document and result framework, it was planned to achieve 71 health facilities in 2023 but later, it was discussed with the donor (KfW) that the project team will cover only 40 health facilities as pilot, while the remaining target are shifted to 2024.</narrative>
  </description>
